---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
const batchCurl = [
  'curl "https://api.barcodenest.com/v1/products/batch"',
  '-H "X-API-Key: YOUR_API_KEY"',
  '-H "Content-Type: application/json"',
  "--data '{\"barcodes\":[\"3017620422003\",\"0036000291452\"]}'",
].join(" \\\n  ");
const curl = `curl "https://api.barcodenest.com/v1/products/3017620422003" \\
  -H "X-API-Key: YOUR_API_KEY"`;
const response = `{
  "barcode": "3017620422003",
  "barcode_type": "EAN-13",
  "canonical_gtin": "03017620422003",
  "valid": true,
  "found": true,
  "product": {
    "name": "Nutella",
    "brand": "Ferrero",
    "quantity": "400 g",
    "image_url": null,
    "allergens": ["milk", "nuts"]
  },
  "source": { "name": "Open Food Facts" },
  "error": null
}`;
---
<DocsLayout title="Barcode Lookup API Endpoint Documentation | BarcodeNest" description="Use the BarcodeNest product lookup endpoint for UPC-A, EAN-8, EAN-13 and GTIN-14 barcodes, with curl and JSON examples." heading="Look up a product by barcode." intro="Validate a UPC, EAN, or GTIN and retrieve an indexed product with one authenticated request." current="lookup">
  <section><h2>Endpoint</h2><p><code class="inline-code">GET /v1/products/&#123;barcode&#125;</code></p><p>The endpoint accepts a supported barcode as a URL path parameter. It validates the length and check digit, derives a canonical GTIN-14 value, and searches the product index.</p><CodeBlock label="cURL request" code={curl} language="bash" /></section>
  <section><h2>Supported formats</h2><table class="status-table"><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Digits</th><th>Canonical behavior</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>EAN-8</td><td>8</td><td>Left-padded to GTIN-14</td></tr><tr><td>UPC-A / GTIN-12</td><td>12</td><td>Left-padded to GTIN-14</td></tr><tr><td>EAN-13 / GTIN-13</td><td>13</td><td>Left-padded to GTIN-14</td></tr><tr><td>GTIN-14</td><td>14</td><td>Used as supplied</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only ASCII digits are accepted. A supported length is not enough: the identifier must also have a valid check digit.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Successful response</h2><CodeBlock label="200 response" code={response} language="json" /><p>Product attributes are optional because source records vary. A found product can still have missing or <code class="inline-code">null</code> fields.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Look up multiple barcodes in one API request</h2><p>Send up to 100 barcodes in the <code class="inline-code">barcodes</code> array to <code class="inline-code">POST /v1/products/batch</code>. Use strings to preserve leading zeros. The response contains one result per input, in the same order.</p><CodeBlock label="Batch cURL request" code={batchCurl} language="bash" /><p>Each submitted barcode counts as one lookup unit. See the <a href="/docs/rate-limits/">rate-limit and quota guide</a> for details.</p></section>
  <section><h2>What happens when a barcode lookup finds no match?</h2><p>A valid barcode can return no product match. For a single lookup, the API returns <code class="inline-code">404 product_not_found</code>. A batch response reports the miss on that item with <code class="inline-code">valid: true</code> and <code class="inline-code">found: false</code>. Invalid input returns <code class="inline-code">400 invalid_barcode</code> on the single endpoint. See the <a href="/docs/errors/">error reference</a> for more cases.</p></section>
<section><h2>Check an identifier before integration</h2><p><a href="/barcode-validator/">Try the free barcode validator</a> to check supported lengths, the final check digit, and the canonical GTIN-14 representation in your browser.</p></section>
<p>For a complete import example, see the <a href="/blog/batch-barcode-lookup-api/">batch barcode lookup guide</a>.</p>
<p><a href="/blog/barcode-lookup-php/">Build a PHP barcode lookup with cURL</a>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
